{
  "issue": 2007,
  "what": "The Update surface rendered from production builds of this branch, measured in headless Chrome at 1440x900, 1280x800 and 390x844 (tall variants at 1900 and 2600 px high), light and dark, en and uk.",
  "checkout": "A git-archive export made into a git checkout, started by bin/cli.mjs under an isolated root, against a local bare remote three to six commits ahead. The update, the web restart and the runtime-host restart were real: a release worktree was built with bun install and bun run build, and the launcher restarted each process onto it.",
  "managed": "The final build started with next start against a stub runtime host that answers the deployment reads and requests and walks the host's phase names on a timer; one deployment succeeded and one rolled back at the health check.",
  "measure": "overflowX: html scrolls sideways; unscrolledOverflow: an element inside the surface wider than its box without a scroller; clippedButtons: a button outside the viewport; overlaps: two text leaves whose ink intersects, each rect clipped by its overflow ancestors. The latest measurement per frame is kept; the first running-state frames were re-measured after the clip was added. One running-state frame (1280, dark, uk) was measured only before that clip and is left out.",
